    22	
    23	## Measured semantics — out of scope
    24	
    25	These properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` record the measured semantics that hook features specify against. The `onError` boundary remains out of scope; issue #93 defines the aggregate usage delivered after tool rounds.
    26	
    27	- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
    28	- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits and receives `TurnUsage`, the summed provider-call usage for the entire turn, so tool rounds are included in a deployer's billing or audit total ([validated by: reports the summed usage from every provider call in a turn with two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L44)).
    29	- Each reported provider call contributes its input, output, and total token fields to that turn-level sum ([validated by: sums usage reported by each provider call in a tool turn](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L550)).
    30	- Missing usage on a provider call does not discard the totals from calls that reported it, while a turn with no reported usage remains `undefined` ([validated by: counts reported rounds while leaving a turn with no reported usage undefined](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L67)).
    18	## Schema compilation
    19	
    20	- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time; an uncompilable schema causes `register` to throw synchronously with a message that names the tool, so a broken schema fails at startup rather than mid-conversation ([validated by: throws at register time when the inputSchema is uncompilable and the message names the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L70)).
    21	- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` is resolved on each `execute` call; the schema validated against is the schema returned by that call, not the one resolved at `register` time ([validated by: validates each call against the schema the definition function returns at that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L81)).
    22	
    23	## Orchestrator integration
    24	
    25	- A validation failure becomes a tool result (not a thrown error), so the orchestrator delivers the rejection text to the model and the model can attempt a corrected call; `DEFAULT_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS = 5` is the bound that stops a retry cycle from spinning ([validated by: resolves processMessage and makes the validation-rejection text visible to the provider on the next round](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L575)).
    26	
    27	## Out of scope
    28	
    29	Validating tool output, hallucination detection, per-tool authorisation, retry and rate limiting around tool execution, and the `Unknown tool: <name>` throw becoming a tool result (tracked separately).
